  "body": "#1071: a Thread op's helix runs the thread depth H = 0.5413 x pitch past the declared hole, which is the thread's minor circle (what CAD draws of a tapped hole), by design (`machining2d::thread_mill`). The verify read that hole as a wall the cutter must keep `r` from, so every matched thread mill was blocked.\n\nThat covered the stock source too, which the issue thought was unaffected: the same thread from `SrcRef::Stock` had 52 gouges and 21 crossing pairs. `mill2d_c` never asserted the warnings, so no thread mill could post from any source.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0, PROCESS_VERSION 16; branched on upstream main 23c62044.\n\n## What changed\n\nThree laws convicted a matched thread, and each is fixed narrowly.\n\n- **Law (b), the rim.** The Thread arm now moves each declared hole's rim out to the major circle (declared radius + H), after the region is built (`material_source::major_rims`). This covers every source and the area-controlled region. A loop that is the hole's minor rim (ours, or the model's own for a through hole) gives way to it; every other wall stays.\n- **The containment solid law.** It read the model's minor wall, and the face the hole opens through, as part to keep. A new `sim::verify::thread_bore` (and `solid_hits_threaded`) excuses a hit only when both of these hold:\n  - the facet is the thread's own material: the minor wall (near-vertical, every vertex on the declared circle within max(2 % r, 0.1 mm)), or a facet with a vertex on that circle lying wholly at or above the hole's entry (the mouth);\n  - the swept cutter stays inside the major cylinder: the farther tip end's radius plus the atom's radius is at most the major radius plus the allowance.\n\n  Floors, walls of another radius, other holes and any cut past the major circle still convict. `solid_hits` is unchanged: it calls the threaded form with no bores.\n- **Law (a), crossings.** The retract runs the ride backwards at feed. The reversed arcs put their chord joints a last bit off their twins, and `proper_cross` excused a touch only at an exactly zero orientation. So each shared joint, and each collinear overlap, read as a crossing.\n\n  Now chords that only touch (an endpoint within 1 nm of the other chord's line) are no crossing. A real crossing keeps every endpoint off the other line. This is the one change that reaches every operation's verify, so the whole batch tier was run (below). A parallel-only guard was tried first: it removed 5 of the 21 pairs, and the rest were the joint touches.\n- Two functions now take eight arguments (`SolidIndex::hits`, `contain_into`). They carry `#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]` with a reason, as ten others in `sim` already do.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1071-thread-mill-rim.md`.\n\n## How it was tested\n\nNew pinning tests:\n- `crates/app/tests/thread_mill_rim.rs` (a 6 mm Tap-form thread mill, pitch 1, model-sourced unless named):\n  - `a_matched_thread_mill_in_air_verifies_clean`: the issue's cavity fixture (#1073's block). Before the fix: 52 gouges and 21 crossing pairs.\n  - `a_matched_thread_mill_in_a_drilled_hole_verifies_clean`: a block with a real r 5 blind hole, 96-gon. Before the fix: the gouges came back from the solid law at the wall and the mouth.\n  - `a_stock_sourced_thread_mill_verifies_clean_too`.\n  - `a_thread_whose_major_circle_reaches_a_wall_convicts`: the major circle is 0.24 mm into the cavity wall; the minor circle is clear of it.\n  - `a_thread_declared_wider_than_the_models_hole_convicts`: the model drilled r 4.5, declared r 5.\n  - `a_thread_taken_below_the_models_hole_floor_convicts`: floor declared at Z 9, model floor at Z 10.\n- `crates/sim/tests/crossing_retrace.rs`:\n  - `a_helix_run_back_over_its_own_trace_is_no_crossing`: three ride/retrace shapes, all-pairs and bucketed. It fails with the touch guard removed, which was checked.\n  - `a_real_crossing_still_reads_as_one_at_any_angle`: 90 degrees down to 0.001 rad.\n\nGates:\n- `cargo xtask gate batch` on c770b35c (18.3 min): every test suite green.\n  - geometry, cl, tools, post, sim (with `crossing_buckets`), motion (slow suites included), app (`center_cut_multiaxis` included), ui.\n  - clippy failed only on the two eight-argument functions. With the `#[allow]` (head commit), `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n- On the head, both pinning suites were rerun: green.\n- No snapshot PNG touched.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No posted thread program was run on a machine or simulator.\n- The thread flanks are not modelled: the whole minor-to-major annulus is read as removable (#986 owns the form).\n- A tilted-frame (indexed) thread uses the same code path, but no test pins it.\n- #1073's `coarse_rims::a_thread_mill_reads_the_same_near_the_bound_as_at_full_fidelity` lives on that open PR. When both land it can tighten to `== Vec::new()`, as #1071 asks.\n\nChangelog: Thread milling: a thread mill matched to its hole verifies clean and can be posted. The gouge checks now read the thread's major circle, and the retract is no longer read as a crossing (#1071)\n\nEffort: high (the issue's label). Not escalated.\n\nFixes #1071\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
